.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH g-notes 1  "g-notes " 
.SH NAME
g\-notes \- Manage private review notes left from `g diff`\*(Aqs `c` key
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBg\-notes\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage private review notes left from `g diff`\*(Aqs `c` key.
.PP
These notes live in the local SQLite DB and are never published to GitHub.  Use `g diff` (and the `c` key inside the TUI) to create them; this command surfaces list/edit/delete/clear operations from outside the TUI.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
g\-notes\-list(1)
List every saved note in this repo (newest first)
.TP
g\-notes\-show(1)
Show a single note by id — prints the body and its anchor
.TP
g\-notes\-edit(1)
Edit the body of an existing note in `$EDITOR`
.TP
g\-notes\-delete(1)
Delete a single note by id
.TP
g\-notes\-clear(1)
Delete all notes for a given file (or every note when no path is given). Requires `\-\-force` to actually run — protects against fat\-finger typos
.TP
g\-notes\-publish(1)
Publish a saved private note to the GitHub PR for the current branch
.TP
g\-notes\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
